WEBVTT

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.349
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Thursday the thirtieth. Have we got everyone who's in?</v>

00:00:08.839 --> 00:00:11.289
<v Fiona Doyle>Think so. Tomasz is there, just muted.</v>

00:00:12.869 --> 00:00:17.070
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, I'm here. Headset button and Teams button. Always the wrong one.</v>

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:20.679
<v Marcus Hale>We got the sigh before you muted it, mind.</v>

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.269
<v Tomasz Nowak>That was the chair.</v>

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:31.109
<v Sarah Okafor>The furniture, I hope. Jamie Brennan and Olumide Adeyemi are absent today, so it's us six.</v>

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:37.020
<v Aisha Begum>Before we start properly, there's a birthday cake in the office. Already cut, if anyone's wondering.</v>

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.789
<v Callum Reid>That explains the queue past the printer.</v>

00:00:43.229 --> 00:00:46.030
<v Fiona Doyle>More interest in that than the biscuits, anyway.</v>

00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:53.299
<v Sarah Okafor>Anything's better than watching the football last night. Honestly, ninety minutes of my life.</v>

00:00:54.159 --> 00:00:55.909
<v Marcus Hale>You stayed till the end?</v>

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:00.070
<v Sarah Okafor>Unfortunately. Right, enough of my poor decisions. Quick updates first.</v>

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:01.689
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, go on.</v>

00:01:03.759 --> 00:01:11.109
<v Sarah Okafor>I can't send the shift handover report round yet. I'm waiting on the permit to be signed, so that's held up.</v>

00:01:13.079 --> 00:01:14.280
<v Fiona Doyle>Ah, right. Understood.</v>

00:01:16.469 --> 00:01:20.319
<v Callum Reid>My near-miss write-up at line three is all done. All fine.</v>

00:01:22.109 --> 00:01:23.310
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Reidy.</v>

00:01:24.219 --> 00:01:27.019
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sorry, bit of a crackle at my end.</v>

00:01:28.049 --> 00:01:29.250
<v Marcus Hale>You're clear now.</v>

00:01:31.209 --> 00:01:35.760
<v Sarah Okafor>And I already swapped the filter on the water ring yesterday. That's sorted.</v>

00:01:36.359 --> 00:01:37.560
<v Tomasz Nowak>Lovely.</v>

00:01:38.549 --> 00:01:39.950
<v Aisha Begum>Right, what's new, then?</v>

00:01:42.129 --> 00:01:51.579
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll go to the hydraulics lot to pick up the replacement parts for the Injection Moulding Line 3 at half two. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:01:51.969 --> 00:01:53.719
<v Tomasz Nowak>You're collecting them yourself, boss?</v>

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:55.890
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, I'll do the collection.</v>

00:01:57.569 --> 00:02:00.370
<v Fiona Doyle>Half two is when you're going over, yeah?</v>

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:05.079
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, at half two. Not a rush trip now.</v>

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:11.259
<v Callum Reid>Fair enough. Otherwise everyone hears 'replacement parts' and assumes it's a panic.</v>

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:14.259
<v Tomasz Nowak>Usually accompanied by someone standing behind you.</v>

00:02:16.419 --> 00:02:17.819
<v Sarah Okafor>I feel very seen.</v>

00:02:19.009 --> 00:02:20.759
<v Aisha Begum>It's the folded arms, boss.</v>

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:23.580
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, moving swiftly on.</v>

00:02:25.039 --> 00:02:29.590
<v Callum Reid>Yeah so, I'll book a contractor to look at the IM2 this morning.</v>

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:36.210
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Reidy. Whenever you get a chance this morning, no need to drop everything.</v>

00:02:37.409 --> 00:02:38.610
<v Callum Reid>Yep, that's fine.</v>

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:45.069
<v Fiona Doyle>That's the booking this morning, not expecting someone through the gate this morning?</v>

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.460
<v Callum Reid>Exactly. I'll make the booking. Haven't promised an arrival time.</v>

00:02:51.639 --> 00:02:54.090
<v Fiona Doyle>Good, that's what I thought you meant.</v>

00:02:54.789 --> 00:02:56.889
<v Marcus Hale>Contractor teleportation's still a bit unreliable.</v>

00:02:58.889 --> 00:03:00.289
<v Tomasz Nowak>Especially with the toolbox.</v>

00:03:00.979 --> 00:03:06.580
<v Fiona Doyle>While we're on timings, I'll schedule downtime for the Engel with production this afternoon. Normal priority.</v>

00:03:08.169 --> 00:03:13.069
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, Fi, I talked over the end there. You're doing the scheduling this afternoon?</v>

00:03:14.099 --> 00:03:19.699
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah. That's when I'll agree the downtime with production, not saying the machine's stopping this afternoon.</v>

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.400
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine, Fi. Normal priority is right.</v>

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:29.060
<v Aisha Begum>Useful distinction. I heard it the other way round for a second.</v>

00:03:30.379 --> 00:03:32.830
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, sorry. First coffee hasn't quite landed.</v>

00:03:34.879 --> 00:03:43.979
<v Sarah Okafor>One more thing: the monthly fire alarm test needs running at half two. Not an emergency but don't let it slip. Anyone able to take that?</v>

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:46.539
<v Marcus Hale>Um...</v>

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:49.009
<v Callum Reid>I can't take that one.</v>

00:03:50.659 --> 00:03:52.060
<v Tomasz Nowak>Nor me, I'm afraid.</v>

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.069
<v Fiona Doyle>Sorry, no.</v>

00:03:56.449 --> 00:03:58.199
<v Aisha Begum>I can't commit to that.</v>

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:01.080
<v Marcus Hale>No, sorry, neither can I.</v>

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:10.020
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. I can't cover it with the collection either. No owner for the fire alarm test, then; it still needs doing at half two.</v>

00:04:10.669 --> 00:04:12.419
<v Callum Reid>Yeah. Not an ideal clash.</v>

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:16.319
<v Sarah Okafor>No. Okay, that's where we are. Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:17.889
<v Tomasz Nowak>Cheers.</v>

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.850
<v Marcus Hale>See you in a bit.</v>
